[20.397444, "o", ">    args:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.39746, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.397492, "o", "     - \"--unbuffered\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.397511, "o", "> "]
[20.397543, "o", "     - \"--argjson min_count 5\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.397562, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.397579, "o", "> "]
[20.397596, "o", "     - \"--tab\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.397613, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.397634, "o", "   ```\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.397652, "o", "   \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.397787, "o", "   '\"'\"'/app/jq_args.yaml'\"'\"' will be used to construct and execute a single jq command as follows:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.397806, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.398007, "o", "   `jq $(yq -r '\"'\"'.args[]'\"'\"' /app/jq_args.yaml) \"$(yq -r '\"'\"'.filter'\"'\"' /app/jq_args.yaml)\" /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json`\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.398021, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.39804, "o", ">    \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.398056, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.398132, "o", "   For the example above, the constructed command would be:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.398149, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.39832, "o", "   `jq --unbuffered --argjson min_count 5 --tab '\"'\"'group_by(.address.city)'\"'\"' /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json`\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.398335, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.39835, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.398365, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.398383, "o", "   This means:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.398398, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.398498, "o", "   1. All arguments in the '\"'\"'args'\"'\"' list will be passed directly to jq\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.398518, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.398609, "o", "   2. The filter string will be passed as the jq filter expression\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.398624, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.398643, "o", "> "]
[20.398732, "o", "   3. The input file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' is fixed and will be used as input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.398749, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.398856, "o", "   4. The output will be redirected to '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.398877, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.398984, "o", "   5. jq will be executed exactly once with all these components\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.399003, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.399018, "o", "   \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.399048, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.399116, "o", "   Requirements for the YAML file:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.399249, "o", "   - The '\"'\"'args'\"'\"' list should contain complete jq arguments, with both flags and their values (if any)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.399266, "o", "> "]
[20.399341, "o", "   - Each argument should be a separate string in the list\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.399355, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.399491, "o", "   - For flag-only arguments, include just the flag (e.g., '\"'\"'--unbuffered'\"'\"', '\"'\"'--tab'\"'\"')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.399506, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.399687, "o", "   - For arguments with values, include both the flag and value as a single string (e.g., '\"'\"'--argjson min_count 5'\"'\"')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.399822, "o", "   - Do not include the jq command itself, the filter expression, or file paths in the args list\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.399842, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.400019, "o", "   - File paths other than the required input file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' and output redirections should not appear in the args\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.400035, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.400156, "o", "   - The filter should be a single string containing the complete jq filter expression\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.400172, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.400187, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.400555, "o", "**Note on examples below**: In the following Data Schema sections, all content following the '\"'\"'#'\"'\"' symbol is just explanatory commentary and will NOT appear in the actual JSON files. These comments are only provided to clarify the structure and requirements.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.400588, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.400617, "o", "**Input Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.400636, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.400774, "o", "The input JSON file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' is an array of user objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.40079, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> [\r\n"]
[20.400804, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.400819, "o", ">   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.400842, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.400939, "o", "    \"id\": 1,                  # Unique numeric identifier for the user\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.400957, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.401048, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",   # User'\"'\"'s unique username (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.401063, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.40116, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # User'\"'\"'s email address (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.401179, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.401291, "o", "    \"status\": \"active\",       # User status: '\"'\"'active'\"'\"' or '\"'\"'inactive'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.40131, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.401439, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02T20:59:10.109812Z\",  # ISO 8601 timestamp (UTC) of the last login\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.401455, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.40159, "o", "    \"roles\": [\"admin\", \"editor\"]  # Array of roles assigned to the user (may be empty)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.401636, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.401664, "o", "  ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.401696, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.401716, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.401733, "o", "**Output Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.401749, "o", "> "]
[20.401925, "o", "The output JSON file '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"' must be an array of objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.401965, "o", "[\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.402065, "o", "    \"user_id\": 1,                 # Derived from '\"'\"'id'\"'\"' in input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.402087, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.402162, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",       # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.402178, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.402194, "o", "> "]
[20.402258, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.402274, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.402293, "o", "> "]
[20.402383, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02\",   # Formatted from '\"'\"'last_login'\"'\"' in input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.4024, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.402501, "o", "    \"role_count\": 2,              # Count of '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' from input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.402518, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.402537, "o", "> "]
[20.402665, "o", "    \"primary_role\": \"admin\"       # If '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' is empty, this must be null (JSON null, not \"null\")\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.402684, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.402701, "o", ">   },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.402718, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.402737, "o", "  ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.402754, "o", "]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.402773, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.402796, "o", "**Requirements**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.402812, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.40283, "o", "> "]
[20.40299, "o", "- You must use jq to perform this transformation. Using other programming languages (e.g., Python, Ruby) is strictly prohibited.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.403008, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.403113, "o", "- Ensure that the output JSON is properly formatted with 2-space indentation.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.403127, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.403146, "o", "> "]
[20.403254, "o", "- The output file must be created at the exact path '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.403277, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
