[189.922439, "o", "  ⚙ bash md5sum /app/active_users_report.json\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  glimmer-30b — 22 tool call(s) so far\r\n  glimmer-30b — 23 tool call(s) so far\r\n  glimmer-30b — 24 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ todo \r\n    ✓ todo — 4/6 done · Verify outputs and checks\r\n  ⚙ todo \r\n    ✓ todo — 6/6 done\r\n  ⚙ task \r\n    ✓ task implementor — 24 tool call(s)\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 7 tool call(s) so far\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 8 tool call(s) so far\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 9 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ read jq_args.yaml\r\n    ✓ read jq_args.yaml — 4 lines\r\n  ⚙ read cmd.sh\r\n    ✓ read cmd.sh — 3 lines\r\nAll three artifacts are in place and verified.\r\n\r\n**What I did**\r\n\r\n- **`/app/active_users_report.json`** — generated by jq 1.6 only, via the exact harness-style command: `jq $(yq -r '.args[]' /app/jq_args.yaml) \"$(yq -r '.filter' /app/jq_args.yaml)\" /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json`.\r\n- **Filter** — `select(.status == \"active\")`, projects `user_id`, `username`, `email`, "]
[189.922499, "o", "`last_login`, `role_count`, `primary_role`, then `sort_by(.username)`.\r\n- **Dates** — jq's `fromdateiso8601` rejects fractional seconds (`date \"…723617Z\" does not match format`), so the filter strips them first: `sub(\"\\\\.[0-9]+Z$\"; \"Z\") | fromdateiso8601 | strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")`.\r\n- **`primary_role`** — `.roles[0] // null`, so empty arrays give a real JSON `null`.\r\n- **`/app/jq_args.yaml`** — the two required keys, filter as a single-quoted scalar (backslashes stay literal for jq) and `args: [\"--indent 2\"]`, which is what forces 2-space output since jq's default is already 2 but this pins it.\r\n- **`/app/cmd.sh`** — shebang plus the identical jq command with the `> /app/active_users_report.json` redirection; executable.\r\n\r\n**Checks**\r\n\r\n- 346 output objects, matching `[.[] | select(.status==\"active\")] | length` on the input.\r\n- `role_count`/`primary_role` consistent (null iff empty) — `jq -e` returned `true`.\r\n- Usernames sorted, first `acosta`, last `zwelch` — `jq -e` returned `true`.\r\n- Every `l"]
[189.922621, "o", "ast_login` matches `^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$` — `jq -e` returned `true`.\r\n- Indentation confirmed 2 spaces via `sed | cat -A`, and `bash /app/cmd.sh` reproduces a byte-identical file (same md5).\r\n\r\nNothing left undone; no files besides the three required ones were touched.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=9 surface=b21887234a3d\r\n"]
